Subject: [PATCH 17/22] L8/D20: bnhgq2/wrap_overflow.py, per-quantizer WRAP
 overflow fraction of a saved model on given rows (diagnostic only)

Counts, per WRAP datalane quantizer (names as width_snapshot), the live elements whose
rounded input falls outside the stored [min, max]; 0-bit elements are reported as pruned.
Runs with training=False through a temporary class-level call wrapper, so no range is
touched and outputs are unchanged. Nothing imports it on the training path.
Test: tests/test_wrap_overflow.py (0 on the traced rows, > 0 on a heavier superset,
0 again after a full trace; weights and outputs unchanged).
